    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0445" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d213-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-11">September 11, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum to the
                    President</hi></p>
                <p>I enclose herewith a copy of a telegram from Ambassador Winant, outlining the
                    present status of the work of the European Advisory Commission. There is
                    likewise enclosed a copy of the draft protocol regarding the zones of occupation
                    in Germany and the administration of “Greater Berlin” which is referred to in
                    Ambassador Winant’s telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ull</hi>]</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d213-a1.xml" xpointer="d213-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d213-a2.xml" xpointer="d213-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d213-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d213-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Roosevelt at Quebec by pouch. The Department of State file copies of this
                    memorandum and its two enclosures bear the file numbers 740.00110 EAC/9–1144, <hi rendition="#italic">id</hi>./9–944,
                    and <hi rendition="#italic">id</hi>./8–3144, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
